    <summary>A Chinese input method (pinyin, shuangpin and wubi) built on a shared input engine.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Metasequoia IME (水杉输入法, MSIME) is a Chinese input method for Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS and HarmonyOS. On Windows it is a Text Services Framework input method with its own Server process, a native candidate window and a settings app.

MSIME is short for Metasequoia IME; it has nothing to do with Microsoft IME.

This package runs the released Inno Setup installer silently; the input method is installed machine-wide under Program Files.

## Package parameters

- `/DataDir:` - an empty directory for the input method's data (dictionaries, settings, skins). Without it the installer keeps the directory of an earlier install, or uses `%LOCALAPPDATA%\metasequoiaime`.

Example: `choco install msime --params "'/DataDir:D:\msime-data'"`

## Notes

Uninstalling deletes the input method's data directory, including your own dictionary words, settings and skins. Upgrading keeps it.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>@RELEASE_NOTES_URL@</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="vcredist140" version="14.20" />
      <dependency id="webview2-runtime" />
